sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:logs
  %% kind: process.logs
  autonumber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP
  participant GW as Gateway
  participant A as Node observer
  participant N as Node SSH account
  participant R as Reverb
  CLI->>GW: process:logs <process>
  alt bounded snapshot
    Note over GW: Read bounded log
    GW-->>CLI: Snapshot and request ID
  else Instance container
    GW->>N: Read container journal<br/>one bounded SSH call
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the Gateway builds fixed argv from the resolved Instance and Process; only the bounded lines count comes from the caller
    %%> - the existing Node SSH account reads the journal with host-equivalent output bounds; the Gateway redacts it and records no Operation or workflow
    GW-->>CLI: Snapshot and request ID
  else --follow (CLI or web viewer)
    CLI->>GW: Open viewer lease
    Note over GW: Authorize source<br/>Store inactive lease
    GW-->>CLI: Channel and signature
    CLI->>R: Subscribe to channel
    CLI->>GW: Activate viewer lease
    GW->>A: log-streams.changed
    A->>GW: Fetch active sources
    loop new lines while lease is active
      A->>R: Read-only log observations
      R->>GW: Log batch
      Note over GW: Redact log lines<br/>Keep loss markers
      GW->>R: Viewer log.lines frames
      R-->>CLI: New lines
      CLI->>GW: Renew every 20 s
    end
    Note over CLI: Reopen on reconnect<br/>Read snapshots if offline
    CLI->>GW: Close viewer lease
  end
